Valdery.

218
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:31,280
Come join my happy song.

219
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:39,600
All right.

220
00:16:39,680 --> 00:16:47,220
So imagine you settle down with your bowl of chips and your dip and your beverage and you're going to watch your football, basketball game, whatever.

221
00:16:47,459 --> 00:16:55,000
Game progresses for a while and your team does well or maybe makes a couple of mistakes and things go back and forth for a bit.

222
00:16:55,000 --> 00:17:00,780
But one thing you notice that never, ever happens is the coaches don't go on the field and start playing the game.

223
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:01,740
It just won't happen.

224
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:04,880
So you notice a scout troop is a lot like an athletic team.

225
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:07,319
It's been called, scouting's been called a game with a purpose.

226
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:08,859
We have coaches.

227
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:10,020
That's you and me.

228
00:17:10,220 --> 00:17:10,900
We have players.

229
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:11,940
That's our youth leader.

230
00:17:12,319 --> 00:17:16,240
And the games they play, they're not like an athletic competition.

231
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:19,960
You can consider a meeting or a camping trip or something like that to be a game.

232
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:29,500
Like coaches of an athletic team, scout leaders can't leave the sidelines and start interfering with the game or start playing the game for their team.

233
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:35,200
Now, the only thing they can do is encourage, train, do things on the sidelines during the game.

234
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:38,440
You're going to get a whistle if you cross the sideline.

235
00:17:38,660 --> 00:17:44,180
You know, if a coach is on the field playing, that means that there's a player who is denied the opportunity of playing.

236
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:46,640
And we can't have players just leave the game.

237
00:17:46,840 --> 00:17:48,700
It's not fair to the rest of the team, is it?

238
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:54,600
It takes a lot of experience and wisdom to know where that sideline is in scouting.

239
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:58,440
What side is the coach's side and which side is the team's side.

240
00:17:58,760 --> 00:18:03,100
So we should have a commitment that coaches don't go on the field and that players don't leave the field to play.

241
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:06,760
And I think that's the way a really great scout troop works.

242
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:09,720
It's when we realize our roles and we stick to them.

